ent-ClothingHeadPaddedarmingcap = padded arming cap
    .desc = A padded up arming cap. It might even stop a mace!

ent-ClothingHeadSkullcap = skull cap
    .desc = A steel helmet which covers the top of the head.

ent-ClothingHeadArmet = armet
    .desc = Holy lamb, sacrificial hero, blessed idiot - Psydon endures. Will you endure alongside Him, as a knight of humenity, or crumble before temptation?

ent-ClothingHeadSallet = sallet
    .desc = A steel helmet which covers most of the head, offering superior coverage to the kettle helmet. Preferred by those who intend to clash steel, rather than those who arch-and-bombard from afar.

ent-ClothingHeadKnight = knight's armet
    .desc = A noble knight's greathelm, and the reigning symbol of sixteenth-century nobility. Add a feather to show the colors of your family or allegiance.

ent-ClothingHeadHounskull = hounskull bascinet
    .desc = A bascinet with a conical visor, favored by those with snouts and whiskers. Nestle a feather or length of cloth onto the rim to display your allegiance.

ent-ClothingHeadLeatherHelm = leather helmet
    .desc = A helmet made of leather.

ent-ClothingHeadKettleHelm = kettle helmet
    .desc = A steel helmet which protects the top and sides of the head. Amongst most standing garrisons, it's customary to wrap an orle - cloth, dyed with the Keep's chosen hues - atop its rim.

ent-ClothingHeadNasalHelm = helmet
    .desc = A helmet that doesn't get any more simple in design.
